    "field": "Paleoceanography",
    "problem": "Existing proxies provide scant constraint on past upper ocean oxygen conditions in the vast open Southern Ocean, which hinders the resolution of mechanisms responsible for the well-documented, but much-debated, ice-age atmospheric CO\u2082 decline.",
    "method": "This study applies the Iodine to Calcium (I/Ca) ratio in planktonic foraminifera as a proxy to estimate past dissolved oxygen concentrations, with values less than ~2.5 \u00b5mol mol\u207b\u00b9 indicating the presence of O\u2082-depleted water in the upper ocean.",
    "task": "This paper uses iodine to calcium (I/Ca) ratios in planktonic foraminifera to reconstruct past dissolved oxygen concentrations in the upper Southern Ocean, demonstrating significant oxygen depletion during the last two glacial periods and its potential link to lower ice-age atmospheric CO2 levels.",
